================================================================================
  TFT_eSPI MIGRATION CHANGELOG — TPM408-2.8 (ST7789 + XPT2046)
  Project: ReviewQuest
  Date: 2026
================================================================================

PURPOSE
-------
Migrate the ReviewQuest quiz game display from the Adafruit ST7789 driver
(slow, separate touch library, conflicting build flags) to the TFT_eSPI
library (faster, integrated touch, single config file). Along the way, fix
the TPM408's characteristic color-order and inversion quirks that the
library does not handle out of the box.

Hardware:
  - ESP32 Dev Module
  - TPM408-2.8" TFT (ST7789 driver, 240x320 native, landscape via rotation)
  - XPT2046 resistive touch controller
  - 6 physical buttons (A, B, C, D, Start) + buzzer + 2 LEDs


================================================================================
  PART 1 — PIN CONFLICT DISCOVERY
================================================================================

Problem:
  Touch controller requires GPIO 19 (MISO / T_DO) to send coordinates back
  to the ESP32. But SystemConfig had:
      static constexpr int BUZZER_PIN = 19;
  The buzzer was silently blocking the MISO line — touch worked sometimes,
  failed otherwise.

Change:
  SystemConfig.h:
    -  static constexpr int BUZZER_PIN = 19;
    +  static constexpr int BUZZER_PIN = 13;

Purpose:
  Frees GPIO 19 for the shared SPI MISO line (TFT SDO + XPT2046 T_DO).
  Without this, touch cannot work reliably regardless of library used.


