================================================================================
  PART 4 — TOUCH CALIBRATION
================================================================================

4.1  Symptom
------------
Initial touch used generic calData:
    uint16_t calData[5] = { 285, 3593, 227, 3714, 4 };
Taps landed 20-200 pixels off. Pressing BTN 1 triggered BTN 5. Pressing
the physical left side reported right-side coordinates.

4.2  Calibration process
------------------------
Flashed a temporary calibration sketch that called:
    tft.calibrateTouch(calData, TFT_WHITE, TFT_BLACK, 15);
The library displays 4 crosshair targets; user taps each precisely with
a stylus. After 4 taps, Serial prints the computed calData array.

4.3  Result
-----------
    uint16_t calData[5] = { 361, 3305, 459, 3183, 1 };

Field meanings (landscape):
    [0] = raw X at left edge
    [1] = raw X at right edge
    [2] = raw Y at top edge
    [3] = raw Y at bottom edge
    [4] = rotation/swap flags

4.4  Mirror correction
----------------------
After calibration, touch was accurate in position but still left-right
mirrored. Solution: set
    #define MIRROR_X 0
    #define MIRROR_Y 0
in the sketch, and apply in pollTouch():
    if (MIRROR_X) x = SCREEN_W - 1 - x;
    if (MIRROR_Y) y = SCREEN_H - 1 - y;

Purpose:
  Flips the coordinate system to match the physical panel orientation.
  When the calibration stores raw values in one polarity and the panel
  expects the opposite, this corrects it without recalibrating.


================================================================================
  PART 5 — LIBRARY PRESERVATION (why lib/TFT_eSPI/)
================================================================================

Problem:
  Edits to .pio/libdeps/esp32dev/TFT_eSPI/ were being reverted whenever
  PlatformIO re-scanned libraries or ran a clean build. The .pio/ folder
  is a cache and PlatformIO treats library sources there as immutable.

Solution:
  Copied the entire library into the project:
      mkdir -p lib
      cp -r .pio/libdeps/esp32dev/TFT_eSPI lib/TFT_eSPI
  Edited lib/TFT_eSPI/TFT_Drivers/ST7789_Init.h and
  lib/TFT_eSPI/User_Setup.h instead.

Verification:
  After this change, the build log shows:
      Compiling .pio/build/esp32dev/lib54e/TFT_eSPI/TFT_eSPI.cpp.o
  The lib54e identifier means PlatformIO is compiling from lib/TFT_eSPI,
  not from the .pio cache.

Benefit:
  - Edits survive: pio run -t clean, rm -rf .pio, library updates, and
    fresh git clones of the project.
  - Config is version-controlled with the rest of the project.


